<application>
  <!-- Appearance > Accessibility > Zoom, at 125%.
       
       Paired with KasmVNC's Native Resolution (enable_hidpi, seeded in
       kasmvnc-subpath-fix.html): native resolution renders at the device's real
       pixels, which is sharper and correspondingly smaller, so without this the
       IDE is crisp and unreadable. The two ship together or not at all.

       NotRoamableUiSettings/ideScale is what the Settings UI actually reads and
       writes — verified by changing the setting in a live IDE and finding it
       here. `-Dide.ui.scale` (also set, in the entrypoint's vmoptions) does NOT
       back this control in ASfP 2025.3; it was the obvious-looking lever and it
       left Settings > Zoom untouched at 100%. "Not roamable" is correct for a
       scale: it is a property of the display this session is streamed to. -->
  <component name="NotRoamableUiSettings">
    <option name="ideScale" value="1.25" />
  </component>
</application>
